    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d712">

                <pb facs="0970" n="856" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg856"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.632/72: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Austria</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stockton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-08-26T11:00:00-04:00">August 26, 1930—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>34. 1. Department approves effort to obtain guarantee referred to in last
                    paragraph of your despatch No. 67, August 5.</p>
                <p>2. Please keep Department informed by telegraph.</p>
                <p>3. Should you be unable to persuade the Austrian Government to accept Senate
                    reservation without reduction of term of treaty, would <pb facs="0971" n="857"
                        xml:id="pg857"/> you favor asking for such acceptance even if accompanied by
                    limitation of compulsory term to 1935?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
